{"name":"Hopsack","hex":"#9e8163","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hopsack","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hemp sack used for holding hops.","A coarse, loosely-woven clothing fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hopsack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plain weave","blocks":[{"text":"Plain weave is the most basic of three fundamental types of textile weaves. It is strong and hard-wearing, and is used for fashion and furnishing fabrics. Fabrics with a plain weave are generally strong, durable, and have a smooth surface. They are used for a variety of applications, including clothing, home textiles, and industrial fabrics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Plainweave.svg/330px-Plainweave.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain_weave","wikidata":"Q1153946"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Tabby1asm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Tabby1asm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Structure of plain-woven fabric","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATabby1asm.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Basketweave1sm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Basketweave1sm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Structure of basketweave fabric","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABasketweave1sm.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Warp_and_weft_2.jpg/330px-Warp_and_weft_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wiki